FinanceReasoning — vendored, modified
=====================================

Upstream
    FinanceReasoning: Benchmarking Financial Numerical Reasoning More Credible,
    Comprehensive and Challenging. Tang, E, Ma, He, Liu, Yang, Rong, Li, Ji,
    Huang, Hu, Liu and Zheng. Proceedings of the 63rd Annual Meeting of the
    Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL 2025), pages 15748-15769.
    arXiv:2506.05828

    Upstream ships no LICENSE file. This copy is redistributed for the sole
    purpose of reproducing the evaluation reported in the accompanying paper.
    Contact the upstream authors for licensing terms.

What this benchmark is used for here
    The Hard subset (238 problems) is the evaluation set for every accuracy,
    completion-rate and token number in the paper. The released library of 3,133
    financial functions in data/functions/ is also the seed corpus for
    data/build/, the corpus construction chain described in paper section 4.1.

Modifications made to the upstream release
    config/config.yaml
        Rewritten. Adds a `local-model1` route pointing at the locally served
        vLLM checkpoint under evaluation, a `sampling_eval` block for avg@N /
        pass@k / entropy reporting, and `deepseek-v4-flash` as the answer
        extraction judge. The model catalog is trimmed to those two routes;
        upstream's wider comparison lineup produces no number in this paper.
    utils/llm.py, utils/config.py, utils/openai_batch.py
        Modified for the local vLLM route and for reasoning models that return
        chain-of-thought on a separate response channel.
    mcnemar_test.py
        Added. Paired significance test between two evaluation.json files.

Removed from this distribution
    Not deleted upstream, simply not redistributed here, as the paper's
    chain-of-thought path never invokes them:
        data/documents/         retrieval corpus (95 MB), RAG path only
        static/, index.html     upstream project webpage
        rag_parallel.py         RAG inference entrypoint
        serve_retriever_*.py    retrieval servers
        utils/bm25_utils.py     used only by the retrieval servers
        extract_test.py, test.json
